\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I Vow to thee, my country,
\par all earthly things above,
\par Entire and whole and perfect,
\par the service of my love;
\par The love that asks no question, the
\par love that stands the test,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par That lays upon the altar the dearest
\par and the best;
\par The love that never falters, the love
\par that pays the price,
\par The love that makes undaunted
\par the final sacrifice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. And there's another country, I've
\par heard of long ago,
\par Most dear to them that love her,
\par most great to them that know;
\par We may not count her armies, we
\par may not see her King;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Her fortress is a faithful heart,
\par her pride is suffering;
\par And soul by soul and silently 
\par her shining bounds increase,
\par And her ways are ways of gentleness
\par and all her paths are peace.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

